# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE SAFETY GUARANTEE: this repo is a BLUEPRINT, never a CAMPAIGN.
# Nothing populated may ever be committed. Repo = how to build a campaign vault.
# Box = the actual played campaign, which stays home. If any of these ever
# appear in `git status`, something is wrong — stop and investigate before
# committing. (The Vander campaign lives in a private box — sean-data-vault —
# NOT here.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The book of record and every populated store — a table's real game.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.ledger.jsonl
campaign.db

# A provisioned box, wherever it lands.
/box/
box/
/run/

# The signing keys for rulings/seals — the crypto root, generated locally, 0600.
keys/
*.key
*.pem

# A grown corpus is DATA (a table's canon, house rules, guests) or licensed
# text a table assembled — never the blueprint. The reader ships; the corpus
# stays with whoever grew it.
corpus/
!corpus/.gitkeep

# Anything with a real person's name in it does not belong in a blueprint.
players/
*.private.*

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
